course: dictionary
lesson: 4889
title: Igneous rock
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Igneous is a word for rock that was once melted. Hot melted rock is called magma when it is underground and lava when it flows out on the surface. When that melted rock cools and hardens, it becomes igneous rock.
explain: Context helps you here. «Igneous rocks are "fire rocks": they form when molten rock cools and hardens, either deep underground or on the surface after an eruption.» Molten means melted, so igneous rocks are made from melted rock that has gone hard again.
explain: Igneous is also a family name. «All rocks belong to three families: igneous, sedimentary and metamorphic.» So igneous is one of three kinds of rock, and each kind forms in its own way.
fact: Igneous is an adjective, so it describes a rock: igneous rock.
fact: «Basalt» is a dark, fine-grained igneous rock made from runny lava.
fact: «Granite» is a speckled igneous rock with big crystals, formed deep underground.
fact: Fast cooling gives small crystals, and slow cooling gives big crystals.
exercise: «Igneous rocks are "fire rocks": they form when molten rock cools and hardens.» What does molten mean? | Frozen solid | *Melted, as hot liquid rock | Covered in moss | Very old
exercise: Which of these rocks is igneous? | Sandstone | *Basalt | Chalk
exercise: Find and copy one of the three rock families from «All rocks belong to three families». | cycle | millions | surface | *sedimentary
test: «Basalt is a dark, fine-grained igneous rock made from runny lava.» Basalt has tiny crystals. What does that tell you about how it cooled? | Slowly, deep underground | It never cooled | It was never melted | *Quickly, on the surface
test: «Granite is a speckled igneous rock with big crystals, formed deep underground.» How did granite cool? | *Slowly, deep underground | In a few seconds on the beach | It did not cool at all | Very quickly in the air
exam: Which sentence best describes igneous rock? | Rock made from shells pressed together over time | Rock that is always soft and wet | *Rock formed when hot melted rock cools and becomes hard | Rock that only grows in forests
